  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 fiscal year marks a definitive pivot from multilateral tax consensus to 'Competitive Sovereignty.' The enactment of the U.S. 'One Big Beautiful Bill Act' (OBBBA) codifies an effective tax rate of approximately 14% for foreign market income, creating a structural clash with the OECD's 15% Pillar Two global floor. In trade policy, a landmark February 2026 Supreme Court ruling has stripped executive authority to impose general tariffs via the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA), forcing a strategic retreat to Section 232 national security justifications. Meanwhile, tax administration has entered an era of 'asynchronous-to-real-time' reporting, led by Singapore's 2026-2031 GST e-invoicing mandate and similar digital gateways in emerging markets like Egypt and India.",
